 *    Estacado to the NORTH and an escarpment marking the beginning of the
 *    EDWARDS PLATEAU to the SOUTH. County elevation 2,200–2,550 ft. Soils:
 *    light to very dark loams with some deep clayey subsoils, LIMESTONE
 *    BEDROCK OUTCROPPINGS in the south-central county, considerable lime
 *    accumulation in subsoils. Rainfall 15.88 in/yr, growing season 217
 *    days.
 *  - The spring itself: pool historically ~15 ft deep, discharging over
 *    100,000 gallons a day in the railroad era; the water table dropped
 *    below the outlet and it was depleted by the mid-1920s; the city now
